  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Lay it off and run in behind",
  "description": "A full-pitch pattern without opponents, with a keeper in each goal. A line of centre backs (A) stands on each side of the pitch, with balls. A central midfielder (C) stands in the middle and a striker (B) high up. A plays up to B, who lays it back to C. B curls a run out and in behind an imaginary back line, C plays the ball in behind in front of B, and B carries it towards the box and shoots.\n\nRun the same pattern the other way at the same time from the other line. Rotate: centre back to midfield, midfielder to striker, and the striker collects the ball and joins the other line. Variant: add a passive defender for B to run in behind without being offside.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The ball in behind should be firm and played into the runner's path, not to their feet."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "The striker curves the run and times it through eye contact with the midfielder."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "The midfielder gets free with a V-run and meets the ball at speed."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Take the ball forward with your first touch and look up before you shoot."
    }
  ],
  "locale": "en",
  "phase": "main",
  "difficulty": 3,
